1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,572
What if a trading bot simply couldn't run

2
00:00:02,602 --> 00:00:04,133
off with your money?

3
00:00:04,633 --> 00:00:06,762
We're a small team that has built trading

4
00:00:06,792 --> 00:00:08,875
agents on five chains.

5
00:00:08,905 --> 00:00:11,534
Every time, the hard part wasn't the

6
00:00:11,564 --> 00:00:14,379
trading. It was trust, and we want to fix

7
00:00:14,409 --> 00:00:15,243
that.

8
00:00:15,743 --> 00:00:18,604
Today's bots want your keys, or a balance

9
00:00:18,634 --> 00:00:20,485
they can move however they like.

10
00:00:20,515 --> 00:00:23,306
There's no limit you can see, and no brake

11
00:00:23,336 --> 00:00:25,099
when one goes wrong.

12
00:00:25,598 --> 00:00:28,215
AI agents can now read markets and place

13
00:00:28,245 --> 00:00:31,001
orders. What's missing is control:

14
00:00:31,031 --> 00:00:33,979
who holds the money, and who can stop them.

15
00:00:34,479 --> 00:00:36,411
XORR does three things.

16
00:00:36,441 --> 00:00:38,710
Hire a council of AI agents that vote on

17
00:00:38,740 --> 00:00:41,032
every trade. Limit them with a permission

18
00:00:41,062 --> 00:00:42,355
the chain enforces.

19
00:00:42,385 --> 00:00:44,671
And stop them, with one hold.

20
00:00:48,771 --> 00:00:51,655
On Monad, a block is final in about half a

21
00:00:51,685 --> 00:00:54,465
second, so the council can vote and fill

22
00:00:54,495 --> 00:00:57,414
together. And it's live on testnet:

23
00:00:57,444 --> 00:01:00,293
verified contracts, council rounds filled on

24
00:01:00,323 --> 00:01:02,998
Perpl, and the stop, each with its

25
00:01:03,028 --> 00:01:04,350
transaction.

26
00:01:04,849 --> 00:01:06,897
It's for people who want an agent to trade

27
00:01:06,927 --> 00:01:09,451
for them, without handing it their money.

28
00:01:09,481 --> 00:01:11,437
We'll reach them through Monad's testnet

29
00:01:11,467 --> 00:01:14,571
community, council replays anyone can share,

30
00:01:14,601 --> 00:01:17,688
and traders already on Perpl and Kuru.

31
00:01:18,188 --> 00:01:20,864
XORR. Try it in a browser.

